sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant S as Server

    Note over C,S: exec() — Request/Response
    C->>S: EXEC_REQ { id, endpoint, args }
    S->>C: EXEC_RESP { id, bytes }

    Note over C,S: exec2() — Server Streaming
    C->>S: EXEC2_REQ { id, endpoint, args }
    S->>C: ACCEPT { id }
    loop Stream
        S->>C: EXEC2_RESP { id, bytes }
    end
    S->>C: COMPLETE { id }

    Note over C,S: exec3() — Bidirectional Streaming
    C->>S: EXEC3_REQ { id, endpoint, args }
    S->>C: ACCEPT { id }
    par Client pushes
        C->>S: EXEC3_PUSH { id, bytes }
    and Server responds
        S->>C: EXEC3_RESP { id, bytes }
    end
    C->>S: EXEC3_CLOSE { id }
    S->>C: COMPLETE { id }